From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:01:29 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Report the auto-focus status from the in-focus flag

The stability flag at 0x0725 only signals that the VCM stopped moving,
so the status claimed REACHED whenever the lens settled, even when the
scan failed. The algorithm's verdict is the in-focus flag at 0x07ae -
report REACHED from that, and FAILED when a single-shot scan settles
without finding focus.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 19 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -704,8 +704,8 @@ static u16 hm5065_mili_to_fp16(s32 val)
 static int hm5065_get_af_status(struct hm5065_dev *sensor)
 {
 	struct hm5065_ctrls *ctrls = &sensor->ctrls;
-	u64 is_stable, mode;
-	int ret;
+	u64 in_focus, is_stable, mode;
+	int ret = 0;
 
 	ret = cci_read(sensor->regmap, HM5065_REG_AF_MODE_STATUS, &mode, NULL);
 	if (ret)
@@ -716,17 +716,22 @@ static int hm5065_get_af_status(struct hm5065_dev *sensor)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	ret = cci_read(sensor->regmap, HM5065_REG_AF_IS_STABLE, &is_stable,
-		       NULL);
+	/*
+	 * The stability flag only signals that the lens stopped moving;
+	 * whether a focused position was actually found is the algorithm's
+	 * verdict in the in-focus flag.
+	 */
+	cci_read(sensor->regmap, HM5065_REG_AF_IN_FOCUS, &in_focus, &ret);
+	cci_read(sensor->regmap, HM5065_REG_AF_IS_STABLE, &is_stable, &ret);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (is_stable)
+	if (in_focus)
 		ctrls->af_status->val = V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_REACHED;
-	else if (!is_stable && mode == HM5065_REG_AF_MODE_CONTINUOUS)
+	else if (!is_stable || mode == HM5065_REG_AF_MODE_CONTINUOUS)
 		ctrls->af_status->val = V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_BUSY;
 	else
-		ctrls->af_status->val = V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_IDLE;
+		ctrls->af_status->val = V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_FAILED;
 
 	return 0;
 }
